  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own 'Five Years Financial Summary' multi-year summary table (audited), Solo/Standalone basis. Reporting basis confirmed by matching this dataset's recorded Total Assets against the bank's own separate (Solo) Balance Sheet, which is consistently lower than its Consolidated Balance Sheet (the bank consolidates an Offshore Banking Unit and a brokerage subsidiary, SJIBL Securities Limited) -- directly verified in FY2013, FY2014, FY2020, FY2022 and FY2025 (see sources.json). As a Shariah-based Islamic bank, Shahjalal Islami Bank PLC reports 'Investment' rather than conventional 'Loans and Advances', and 'Classified Investment'/'Non-Performing Investment' rather than 'NPL', consistent with the convention used elsewhere in this dataset for EXIMBANK and FIRSTSBANK. Total Liabilities is not a separate line in the summary table and is calculated as Total Assets minus Total Shareholders' Equity. RESTATEMENT FOUND: Tier 1 Capital for FY2023 is contemporaneously reported as 28,736mn (Total Capital 34,126mn, Capital Surplus 11,464mn, CRAR 15.06%). The FY2024 and FY2025 annual reports' comparative columns both instead show Tier 1 = 28,727mn (Total Capital 34,117mn, Capital Surplus 11,454mn, CRAR 15.05%) -- a trivial ~9-10mn (0.03%) difference, immaterial and below the flag threshold, noted for completeness. Tier 2 Capital (5,391mn) and every Financial Position / Operating Result row are unchanged across all reports. Contemporaneous FY2023 figures kept per project rule.",
